      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Attempt to resolve in any direction. — M1: allow trigonometric-function mix-up or sign error; correct number of terms.\n$F\\cos\\alpha-20\\cos40^\\circ-100\\sin20^\\circ=0$, so $F\\cos\\alpha=49.5229\\ldots$. — A1.\n$F\\sin\\alpha+20\\sin40^\\circ-100\\cos20^\\circ=0$, so $F\\sin\\alpha=81.1135\\ldots$. — A1.\n$F=\\sqrt{49.5229^2+81.1135^2}$. — M1: attempt $F$, with at most one term missing overall.\n$\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}(81.1135/49.5229)$. — M1: attempt $\\alpha$, with at most one term missing overall.\n$F=95.0$, $\\alpha=58.6^\\circ$. — A1; unrounded $95.0364\\ldots$, $58.5943\\ldots^\\circ$.\nAlternative cosine/sine-rule scheme: attempt cosine rule with 100, 20 and a suitable angle. — M1; $F^2=100^2+20^2-2(100)(20)\\cos70^\\circ$. — A1; $F=95.0$. — A1; attempt sine rule. — M1; correct angle relation $\\beta=70^\\circ-\\alpha$ or $\\gamma=40^\\circ+\\alpha$. — A1; $\\alpha=58.6^\\circ$. — A1.\nAlternative resolving directions: $F\\sin(\\alpha+20^\\circ)+20\\sin20^\\circ-100=0$ and $F\\cos(\\alpha+20^\\circ)-20\\cos20^\\circ=0$. — M1 A1 A1; then attempt $F$ and $\\alpha$. — M1 M1; same final answers. — A1.\nTotal: 6.",
